incident-bot: :rotating_light: ALERT: elevated 5xx rate seen on hosted inference (us-east-1). 5m P50 5xx = 3.2% (baseline 0.1%). Investigating.

maria (sre): I'm seeing spikes from runtime-gateway -> runtime-infer-0x with repeated 502/504s. Errors correlate with large streaming jobs and some very high concurrent clients. Logs show upstream OOMs at the model worker.

sam (runtime): Confirmed. GPU memory pressure on a subset of nodes. We have backlog growing in the router -> worker KV cache miss path. Likely continuous batching + long sequences causing eviction thrash.

maria (sre): Live mitigations proposal: 1) soft-rate-limit top 10 noisy API keys to 15 rps 2) disable streaming for non-enterprise keys (fall back to non-streaming responses) 3) reduce default max_tokens to 512 for free/dedicated-hosted tiers 4) enable immediate fallback to smaller quantized variant for model X when queue depth > 50. Thoughts?

lee (devex): From SDK perspective we should push guidance immediately: increase client-side backoff, add idempotency header support, set default retry limits. We can ship a micro-patch to the JS/py SDK with a compatibility flag so apps get behavior opt-in.

priya (cs): I'll notify top 8 customers who show highest error rates. Need exact mitigation text for CS copy. Which keys are being limited?

maria (sre): Limiting keys: api_ABC123, api_XYZ789, api_BIGCLIENT1, api_BIGCLIENT2 (top noisy). We'll roll by policy and monitor. CS message: "We're applying temporary rate shaping to reduce errors; you may see increased client retries — recommended SDK updates below."

sam (runtime): I'll flip routing to quantized-variant as a fallback for queues > 50. Also temporarily disable streaming on router for tier=free to cut down KV churn. That should drop mem pressure within ~2 minutes.

incident-bot: deploy-bot triggered a config push: routing-policy:v2 -> staged, limiters:v1 applied to api_ABC123/api_XYZ789.

dave (oncall): Taking handoff for the next 60m. Action items for me: 1) enforce soft 15rps per-key via ratelimit service 2) apply streaming-disable policy for non-enterprise 3) enable fallback routing 4) coordinate with CS for customer comms. I'll post status updates every 10m.

lee (devex): SDK mitigation guidance (for quick copy into CS):
- Short-term: enable exponential backoff with jitter, set retries=5, initial_delay=100ms, multiplier=2.0, max_delay=10s. Use idempotency keys for non-idempotent calls.
- Medium-term: add support for server-driven Retry-After and client honor for 429/5xx.

lee (devex): Quick code snippet (JS) to share with customers:
```js
// small wrapper for fetch that implements exponential backoff + idempotency header
async function inferWithRetry(url, body, opts = {}) {
  const maxRetries = opts.retries ?? 5;
  const baseDelay = opts.baseDelayMs ?? 100;
  const multiplier = 2;
  const jitter = 0.3;
  const idempotencyKey = opts.idempotencyKey || generateUUID();

  for (let attempt = 0; attempt <= maxRetries; attempt++) {
    try {
      const res = await fetch(url, {
        method: 'POST',
        headers: {
          'Content-Type': 'application/json',
          'X-Idempotency-Key': idempotencyKey,
          ...(opts.headers || {})
        },
        body: JSON.stringify(body)
      });
      if (res.ok) return res.json();
      if (res.status === 429 || res.status >= 500) throw new Error('retryable');
      // non-retryable error -> bubble up
      throw new Error('non-retryable');
    } catch (e) {
      if (attempt === maxRetries) throw e;
      // exponential backoff with full jitter
      const exp = Math.pow(multiplier, attempt) * baseDelay;
      const jitterMs = Math.round(Math.random() * jitter * exp);
      const delayMs = Math.min(exp + jitterMs, 10000);
      await new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, delayMs));
    }
  }
}
```

lee (devex): Also example curl header for idempotency: `curl -H "X-Idempotency-Key: <uuid>" -d '{...}' https://api.redwood.ai/v1/infer`

maria (sre): Operational guidance for on-call teams: 1) prefer soft-shaping before global disables 2) maintain a whitelist for enterprise customers to avoid undue impact 3) monitor queue depth & GPU mem > if fallback doesn't reduce errors in 10m escalate to scale-up.

sam (runtime): Note: disabling streaming reduces KV cache churn but increases per-request peak memory (longer worker lifetimes), so we watch worker count. If mem goes up, we will also reduce `max_tokens` as planned.

priya (cs): Messaging to customers drafted and sent to the impacted accounts. Will include SDK snippet and guidance to upgrade to latest client within next 24h.

dave (oncall): First 10m update: applied soft 15rps limits to noisy keys, streaming disabled for free tier, fallback to quantized variant active. Error rate dropped from 3.2% -> 0.9% in 6m. Continuing to monitor. :white_check_mark:

maria (sre): Good improvement. Keep shaping for 30m then relax incrementally if stable.

lee (devex): I'll open an urgent patch PR for SDKs with a feature-flag default to the recommended retry behavior and backport notes. Link will be in follow-up.

dave (oncall): 30m update: further down to 0.3% 5xx. Leaving soft limits in place for another hour. Handoff to next oncall at 1842113200. Postmortem owner assigned: sam (runtime).

incident-bot: incident resolved?auto-check -> monitors recovered. Closing alert if stable for 60m. :tada:

priya (cs): Thanks team — I'll follow up with customers and include final mitigation timeline.

maria (sre): Postmortem notes: primary cause = workload skew (few noisy keys) + long-sequence streaming causing KV eviction with memory spikes. Action items: improve per-key telemetry, client SDK defaults for backoff, server-side idempotency header support, and automated tier-aware streaming policy.

sam (runtime): Adding a runtime metric to trigger early fallback to quantized model at queue depth 30.

lee (devex): I'll prepare a short 'How to survive rate shaping' FAQ for the docs site with code examples and recommended settings.

deploy-bot: config push successful: ratelimit v1, routing-policy:v2, sdk-patch:branch/retry-defaults opened.

dave (oncall): Handoff complete. Leaving notes in PagerDuty handoff. :white_check_mark:
